Brief: Conrey Theorem 2 (Q = 1) as quoted by BCY; functional-equation transfer to σ⁺ with the δ-split; Littlewood + Jensen; layer cake with (R/L)ν(½,T); optimal P; c*(R); numbers 0.0805 (R → 0) and 0.0527 (κ = 0.6725, R = 1.164).
Verdict: SOUND. "All four steps are correct conditional on the stated critical-line proportion." Littlewood 1/(2π) times Jensen 1/2 gives 1/(4π); mollifier zeros only increase the count; thin strip ∫_{1/2}^{σ+} ν ≤ (R/L)ν(½,T); ν(½,T) = (N − N_0)/2; minimiser P'' = b²P gives b(1 + coth b); equivalent form c*(R) = 1 + (1 − e^{−2R})/(e^{2θR} − 1).
